ACCEPTANCE SCENARIOS

A. MIRRORED SINGLE-CORNER TEST

- Place one wooden block and one angled rafter at the upper-right corner.
- Confirm committed Corner Joint.
- Mirror the arrangement at the upper-left corner.
- Confirm equivalent committed Corner Joint.
- Confirm marker parity.
- Confirm joint-profile parity.

B. SOURCE/TARGET ORDER TEST

For each mirrored corner:

- Move the rafter to the block.
- Move the block to the rafter.

Confirm equivalent final geometry and joint.

C. VISUALLY REASONABLE SUPPORTED ROOF

- Use two equal wooden supports.
- Use two equal opposing rafters.
- Place each lower endpoint near the corresponding upper inner corner.
- Place upper endpoints near one another.
- Confirm roof-assembly preview.
- Confirm both lower relationships and peak relationship.
- Commit.
- Run Test Stability.
- Confirm the roof remains assembled under ordinary gravity if the supports
  themselves remain upright.

D. FREE-STANDING SUPPORTS

- Use two narrow, unanchored support blocks.
- Build the same connected roof.
- Confirm geometry remains connected initially.
- Run Test Stability.
- If supports tip under roof thrust, confirm the roof may collapse naturally.
- Confirm the failure is attributed to support instability rather than a missing
  connection or artificial joint strain.

E. STABLE OR ANCHORED SUPPORTS

- Use stable columns, anchors, or wider supports.
- Build the same roof.
- Confirm ordinary-load stability improves.

F. MISSING LOWER CONNECTION

- Create peak and one lower connection only.
- Confirm preview identifies the unresolved side.
- Test stability.
- Confirm failure or shifting is allowed.

G. FORGIVING CLOSURE

- Build a roof with a small dimensional mismatch.
- Confirm small previewed correction.
- Commit.
- Confirm stress-free rest geometry.
- Test stability.

H. EXCESSIVE MISMATCH

- Create a visibly lopsided arrangement outside tolerance.
- Confirm no automatic large correction.
- Confirm no false committed marker.

I. FINE ADJUSTMENT

- Lock a lower-corner candidate.
- Nudge the piece.
- Confirm candidate remains manageable rather than immovable.
- Commit within tolerance.
- Confirm valid joint.

J. CANCEL AND UNDO

- Begin roof closure and cancel.
- Confirm exact restoration.
- Commit and Undo.
- Confirm all affected transforms and joints restore.
- Redo and confirm no duplicates.

K. RELOAD

- Reload after a committed roof.
- Confirm same geometry and rest state.
- Test stability.
- Confirm no added strain.

L. PROJECTILE IMPACT

- Strike the ordinary-load-stable roof.
- Confirm joints may flex, strain, or break.
- Confirm cosmetic caps disappear when joints break.
- Confirm physics remains authoritative.

